{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'idempoten|merchantReference.*unique|duplicate' /tmp/prodigi-reference.html | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"603:    </span><span class=\"nl\">\"idempotencyKey\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">null</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\">\n718:<td><code>idempotencyKey</code></td>\n721:<td>Your personal <a href=\"#order-object-idempotency-key\" title=\"About idempotency keys\">idempotency key</a>.</td>\n1279:<h3 id='order-object-idempotency-key'>Idempotency key</h3>\n1280:<p>The<code>idempotencyKey</code> is an optional property that can help us determine if your order is a duplicate of an earlier order. If not supplied, the order will not be checked for duplicates.</p>\n1282:<p>Most merchants can guarantee that we will only receive one request for one order, so the idempotency key would not be required. For others who may be running distributed systems where it can be harder to guarantee a single request for a single order, the use of the <code>idempotencyKey</code> is recommended: a string that is unique to this order.</p>\n1284:<p>While the idempotency key can be a simple string, we recommended that you use a GUID of some form to avoid clashes. We remember all your idempotency keys indefinitely, so you need a key of sufficient complexity.</p>\n1286:<p>Internally, the idempotency key is scoped to your account, so another merchant&#39;s key will never conflict with yours.</p>\n1289:We use <code>idempotencyKey</code> to check for duplicates rather than <code>merchantReference</code> as it's not uncommon for merchants to order reprints of an order using the same <code>merchantReference</code>.\n1399:        </span><span class=\"nl\">\"idempotencyKey\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">null</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\">\n1510:<td>Order with the same idempotency key already exists. The new order has not been created, and we have returned the existing order.</td>\n1528:        </span><span class=\"nl\">\"idempotencyKey\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">null</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\">\n1817:        </span><span class=\"nl\">\"idempotencyKey\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">null</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\">\n1952:        </span><span class=\"nl\">\"idempotencyKey\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">null</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\">\n2376:        </span><span class=\"nl\">\"idempotencyKey\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">null</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\">\n3605:        </span><span class=\"nl\">\"idempotencyKey\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">null</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\">\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
