{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_112","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"stripe webhook_endpoints create --help | sed -n '1,240p'\"","aggregated_output":"Usage:\n  stripe webhook_endpoints create [--param=value] [-d \"nested[param]=value\"]\n\nExamples:\n  # required fields\n  $ stripe webhook_endpoints create --enabled-events <string> --url <string>\n\n[Agent guidance]\n  If you do not have an account: run stripe sandbox create (provisions a claimable sandbox without a browser).\n  If you already have a key: use --api-key (or set STRIPE_API_KEY).\n  Use -d to set nested params, e.g. -d \"metadata[key]=value\".\n  Run stripe --map to quickly see all available commands.\n  Run stripe resources to discover all available API resources.\n  Run stripe [resource] --help to see operations and required/common parameters for a resource.\n  Run stripe help [resource] [operation] to see the full parameter list for a specific operation.\n  Use --stripe-account to make requests on behalf of connected accounts.\n\nRequest Parameters:\n      --api-version 2011-01-01|2011-06-21|2011-06-28|2011-08-01|2011-09-15|...\n          Events sent to this endpoint will be generated with this Stripe\n          Version instead of your account's default Stripe Version\n      --description <string>\n          An optional description of what the webhook is used for\n      --enabled-events <string>  [can be specified multiple times]\n          The list of events to enable for this endpoint\n      --url <string>\n          The URL of the webhook endpoint\n\n  ... and 1 more parameters (stripe help webhook_endpoints create)\n\nFlags:\n  -c, --confirm                 Skip the warning prompt and automatically\n                                confirm the command being entered\n      --dark-style              Use a darker color scheme better suited\n                                for lighter command-lines\n  -d, --data stringArray        Data for the API request\n      --dry